  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">West Bengal Health System Reform Program Operation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed Program will support health sector reforms to address a dual burden of disease in a large, poor state in the Indo-Gangetic plains severely affected by climate change.  It builds on the Bank&apos;s earlier engagement in West Bengal as well as the current health sector priorities in India.  The proposed Program aims to catalyze large-scale health sector reforms to enhance access, quality and equity to benefit millions of people.This is a hybrid operation that uses both the PforR and IPF instruments. The IPF component is a very small part of the Program and is focused only on technical assistance activities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve utilization of health services, enhance quality of care and reduce inequities in maternal and adolescent health in West Bengal</narrative>
  </description>
